==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Zory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Zory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 95% HP:
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 92% HP:
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This [[Zombie Outbreaks|Outbreak]] won't be crazy at first, but when you hit the base you will need to deal with the Zories' burrows and protect any damage dealers you already spawned. If you have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] and are worried about losing them, save them until after the Zories have already burrowed.

Once Mooth spawns, your army will get knocked back by the boss shockwave and a couple Zrocos will spawn too. The knockback will make the Zory and Zroco harder to deal with as they will continue to push into your base and burrow into your backline. If they get past your meatshields and kill your DPS you may just have to retry. Remember, [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] outranges everything but Mooth.

